@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:global.subcomponent.file_upload_input a ds:Subcomponent;
    ds:name "FileUploadInput";
    ds:summary "The file-attaching control inside [FileUploadField](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-V7eYe7_ATI). It has two parts: a drop area where users drag files or choose them with the button, and a list of the selected files. Each file in the list shows its name, optional size, optional thumbnail, upload status, and the remove and retry actions. If a file fails validation, a warning or error message appears under its tile.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "Initial Anatomy DSL\n\n```yaml\n---\n# Authored 2026-09-13 from @canonical/react-ds-global-form\n# src/lib/subcomponent/FileUploadInput/styles.css on .ds.input.file-upload and\n# its child selectors (> .drop-zone, its hidden native input, > .file-list and\n# the five parts of a .file-item), with the tokens it reads from src/index.css.\n# The stylesheet corrects the notation: the file items live in a list container,\n# not directly under the root.\nnode:\n  uri: global.subcomponent.file_upload_input\n  styles:\n    layout.type: flex\n    layout.direction: column\n    # The gap reads --form-group-gap, then --space-100 (and --density-space-sm\n    # inside a density scope): none of the three is declared.\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: drop area\n        styles:\n          layout.type: flex\n          layout.align: center\n          layout.justify: center\n          layout.boxSizing: border-box\n          appearance.border.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n          appearance.border.style: dashed\n          appearance.border.color: color.border\n          appearance.radius: dimension.radius.small\n          appearance.background: color.foreground.input\n          typography.color: color.text.muted\n          interaction.cursor: pointer\n          motion.property: border-color, background-color\n          # The hover fill reads --hover--color-foreground-input first, a computed\n          # state variable that no stratum declares as a symbol.\n          appearance.background@hover: color.foreground.input.hover\n          appearance.border.color@focus: color.focusRing\n          # A `.danger` field — a failed validation — repaints the dashed border.\n          appearance.border.color@invalid: color.border.error\n          appearance.outline.style@focus: none\n          appearance.background@disabled: color.foreground.input.disabled\n          interaction.cursor@disabled: not-allowed\n          # Not bound, and why:\n          # - min-height is a calc() over dimension.400 (128px), and the padding\n          #   a calc() that subtracts the border thickness from\n          #   --form-input-padding-block so the total stays on the baseline grid;\n          # - the inline padding reads --form-input-padding-inline, then\n          #   --component-padding-inline: neither is declared;\n          # - the focus ring is a box-shadow at --form-focus-ring-color, and the\n          #   disabled text colour reads the computed --disabled--color-text;\n          # - the transition duration reads --motion-duration-fast, undeclared;\n          # - `.drag-over` takes the focus border and the hover fill, which is a\n          #   variant rather than one of the states.\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: native file input\n              styles:\n                # Visually hidden but kept in the accessibility tree: the drop\n                # area is the affordance, the input is the control.\n                layout.position: absolute\n                size.width: 1px\n                size.height: 1px\n                layout.overflow: hidden\n                typography.whiteSpace: nowrap\n                appearance.border.width: 0\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"1\"\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1\"\n        slotName: default\n    - node:\n        role: file list\n        styles:\n          layout.listStyle: none\n          layout.type: flex\n          layout.direction: column\n          spacing.internal.block.start: 0\n          spacing.internal.block.end: 0\n          spacing.internal.inline.start: 0\n          spacing.internal.inline.end: 0\n          # `margin: 0` zeroes all four sides of the list.\n          spacing.external.block.start: 0\n          spacing.external.block.end: 0\n          spacing.external.inline.start: 0\n          spacing.external.inline.end: 0\n          # The gap reads --form-group-gap, undeclared, as the root's does.\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: file item\n              styles:\n                layout.type: flex\n                layout.align: baseline\n                layout.boxSizing: border-box\n                appearance.border.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n                appearance.border.style: solid\n                appearance.border.color: color.border\n                appearance.radius: dimension.radius.small\n                appearance.background: color.foreground.input\n                spacing.internal.block.start: 0\n                spacing.internal.block.end: 0\n                # The gap reads --form-field-inline-gap and the inline padding\n                # --form-input-padding-inline, and the height\n                # --form-input-height: none of their chains resolves.\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    role: file preview\n                    styles:\n                      size.width: dimension.400\n                      size.height: dimension.400\n                      layout.objectFit: cover\n                      appearance.radius: dimension.radius.small\n                      layout.flex.shrink: 0\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: file name\n                    styles:\n                      layout.flex.grow: 1\n                      layout.flex.shrink: 1\n                      layout.flex.basis: 0%\n                      size.min.width: 0\n                      layout.overflow: hidden\n                      typography.overflow: ellipsis\n                      typography.whiteSpace: nowrap\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: file size\n                    styles:\n                      typography.color: color.text.muted\n                      typography.whiteSpace: nowrap\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: file remove\n                    styles:\n                      appearance.native: none\n                      appearance.border.style: none\n                      appearance.background: none\n                      typography.color: color.text.muted\n                      typography.color@hover: color.text\n                      interaction.cursor: pointer\n                      interaction.cursor@disabled: not-allowed\n                      appearance.opacity@disabled: 0.5\n                      # Its padding (0 0.25rem) is a literal pair the stylesheet\n                      # writes.\n                      spacing.internal.block.start: 0\n                      spacing.internal.block.end: 0\n                      spacing.internal.inline.start: 0.25rem\n                      spacing.internal.inline.end: 0.25rem\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"1\"\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"0..*\"\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n```\n\nRegenerated Anatomy DSL\n\n```yaml\n---\n# The file-attaching part of the field: a drop area and the list of chosen\n# files. Each file item is an anonymous part, since no block names it and the\n# component draws it itself.\nnode:\n  uri: global.subcomponent.file_upload_input\n  styles:\n    layout.type: flex\n    layout.direction: column\n    # 16px between the drop area and the file list.\n    spacing.gap.block: dimension.200\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        role: drop area\n        styles:\n          layout.type: flex\n          layout.direction: column\n          layout.align: center\n          layout.justify: center\n          layout.boxSizing: border-box\n          # The 112px minimum height is not bound: no dimension symbol declares\n          # it, and size.min.height admits symbols only.\n          spacing.internal.block.start: dimension.200\n          spacing.internal.block.end: dimension.200\n          spacing.internal.inline.start: dimension.200\n          spacing.internal.inline.end: dimension.200\n          spacing.gap: dimension.100\n          appearance.border.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n          appearance.border.style: dashed\n          appearance.border.color: color.border\n          appearance.border.color@invalid: color.border.error\n          appearance.border.color@disabled: color.border.disabled\n          appearance.background: color.foreground.input\n          # A file dragged over the area takes this same fill. The DSL has no\n          # drag-over state, so that trigger is not expressed.\n          appearance.background@hover: color.foreground.input.hover\n          appearance.background@disabled: color.foreground.input.disabled\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: helper text\n              styles:\n                typography.font: typography.text.primary\n                typography.color: color.text\n                typography.color@disabled: color.text.disabled\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              uri: global.component.button\n              props:\n                icon: upload\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"1\"\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        role: file list\n        styles:\n          layout.type: flex\n          layout.direction: column\n          spacing.gap.block: dimension.200\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: file item\n              styles:\n                layout.type: flex\n                layout.direction: column\n                spacing.gap.block: dimension.100\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    role: tile body\n                    styles:\n                      layout.type: flex\n                      layout.direction: row\n                    edges:\n                      - node:\n                          role: thumbnail\n                          styles:\n                            # 60x36 gives a 5:3 ratio; the DSL has no aspect-ratio\n                            # key, so only the two dimensions carry it. The height\n                            # matches the tile's, so the item does not grow.\n                            size.width: 60px\n                            size.height: 36px\n                            layout.flex.shrink: 0\n                            layout.overflow: hidden\n                            layout.objectFit: cover\n                        relation:\n                          cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      - node:\n                          role: tile details\n                          styles:\n                            layout.type: flex\n                            layout.direction: row\n                            layout.align: center\n                            layout.flex.grow: 1\n                            spacing.gap: dimension.100\n                            spacing.internal.block.start: dimension.050\n                            spacing.internal.block.end: dimension.050\n                            spacing.internal.inline.start: dimension.150\n                            spacing.internal.inline.end: dimension.050\n                            # The Criticality family reaches the tile through this\n                            # channel: warning and error tint the surface.\n                            appearance.background: [modifier.color.foreground.input, color.foreground.input]\n                          edges:\n                            - node:\n                                role: file info\n                                styles:\n                                  layout.type: flex\n                                  layout.direction: row\n                                  layout.align: center\n                                  layout.flex.grow: 1\n                                  size.min.width: 0\n                                  spacing.gap: dimension.100\n                                edges:\n                                  - node:\n                                      role: file name\n                                      styles:\n                                        typography.font: typography.text.primary\n                                        typography.color: [modifier.color.text.onForegroundSecondary, color.text.onForegroundSecondary]\n                                        # A long name truncates with an ellipsis.\n                                        layout.flex.shrink: 1\n                                        size.min.width: 0\n                                        layout.overflow: hidden\n                                        typography.overflow: ellipsis\n                                        typography.whiteSpace: nowrap\n                                    relation:\n                                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                                  - node:\n                                      role: file size\n                                      styles:\n                                        typography.font: typography.text.secondary\n                                        typography.color: [modifier.color.text, color.text.muted]\n                                        typography.whiteSpace: nowrap\n                                    relation:\n                                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                              relation:\n                                cardinality: \"1\"\n                            - node:\n                                role: status and actions\n                                styles:\n                                  layout.type: flex\n                                  layout.direction: row\n                                  layout.align: center\n                                  # 6px: no symbol declares this step, so it is\n                                  # written as a literal.\n                                  spacing.gap: 6px\n                                edges:\n                                  - node:\n                                      role: file status\n                                      styles:\n                                        layout.type: flex\n                                        layout.direction: row\n                                        layout.align: center\n                                        spacing.gap: dimension.100\n                                      edges:\n                                        - node:\n                                            role: upload progress\n                                            styles:\n                                              typography.font: typography.text.secondary\n                                              typography.color: color.text.muted\n                                          relation:\n                                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                                        # The success, warning and error glyphs are\n                                        # drawn with raw colours that no symbol\n                                        # declares, so their colours are not bound.\n                                        - switch:\n                                            on: internal\n                                            cases:\n                                              - uri: global.subcomponent.spinner\n                                              - node:\n                                                  uri: global.component.icon\n                                                  props:\n                                                    icon: success-fill\n                                              - node:\n                                                  uri: global.component.icon\n                                                  props:\n                                                    icon: warning-fill\n                                              - node:\n                                                  uri: global.component.icon\n                                                  props:\n                                                    icon: error-fill\n                                          relation:\n                                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                                    relation:\n                                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                                  # The buttons read the tile's Criticality family\n                                  # through their own icon channel. The warning and\n                                  # error icon colours placed on a secondary\n                                  # foreground have no channel, so those exact\n                                  # symbols are not bound.\n                                  - node:\n                                      role: file actions\n                                      styles:\n                                        layout.type: flex\n                                        layout.direction: row\n                                        layout.align: center\n                                      edges:\n                                        - node:\n                                            uri: global.component.button\n                                            props:\n                                              icon: change-version\n                                          relation:\n                                            cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                                        - node:\n                                            uri: global.component.button\n                                            props:\n                                              icon: close\n                                          relation:\n                                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                                    relation:\n                                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                              relation:\n                                cardinality: \"1\"\n                        relation:\n                          cardinality: \"1\"\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: validation message\n                    styles:\n                      layout.type: flex\n                      layout.direction: row\n                      layout.align: flex-start\n                      spacing.gap: dimension.050\n                    edges:\n                      - switch:\n                          on: internal\n                          cases:\n                            - node:\n                                uri: global.component.icon\n                                props:\n                                  icon: warning\n                                styles:\n                                  typography.color: [modifier.color.icon, color.icon]\n                                  spacing.external.block.start: dimension.025\n                                  spacing.external.block.end: dimension.025\n                            - node:\n                                uri: global.component.icon\n                                props:\n                                  icon: error\n                                styles:\n                                  typography.color: [modifier.color.icon, color.icon]\n                                  spacing.external.block.start: dimension.025\n                                  spacing.external.block.end: dimension.025\n                        relation:\n                          cardinality: \"1\"\n                      - node:\n                          role: message text\n                          styles:\n                            layout.flex.grow: 1\n                            typography.font: typography.text.secondary\n                            typography.color: [modifier.color.text, color.text.destructive]\n                        relation:\n                          cardinality: \"1\"\n                  relation:\n                    cardinality: \"0..1\"\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"1..*\"\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n```";
    ds:anatomyClassic "Anatomy\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13360-17688&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1\n\nStyling\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13369-21097&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13414-7087&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13414-9043&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13455-6608&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1\n\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/WGHcOmGMEUF9hMAEoRafL8/%F0%9F%93%95-Pragma---documentation-visuals?node-id=13455-6828&t=cEAarkbWU6qDCTl8-1";
    ds:usage "The file-attaching control used inside FileUploadField: a drop area and a list of the selected files. It is not used on its own, only inside a field such as FileUploadField.\n\n## **When to use**\n\n- A user needs to attach one or more existing documents, images, or other files.\n- The input requires a file rather than content entered as text.\n\n## **When not to use**\n\n- The user needs to enter text directly — use [TextInput](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-csRvI-VTpO) or [TextareaInput](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-AhD9dYg2Q9).\n- The user needs to select from a predefined set of options — use [SelectInput](https://docs.superhuman.com/d/_dNyzE_TLZDh#_tugrid-20dWwIHYhx/_rui-xiMRYATXwr).";
    ds:guidelines "";
    ds:tier ds:global;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.needsdesign.
